# DigiSwasthya Product Definition Document (PDD)

# Part 12 — Notifications

---

# Purpose

This section defines every notification DigiSwasthya generates.

For each notification:

- Trigger
- Recipients
- Priority
- Persistence
- Expiry
- Click destination
- Actions available
- Whether it is actionable

Notifications communicate events. They never replace official workflows.

---

# Notification Principles

1. Generated after the business event succeeds.
2. Failure to notify must not roll back the business event by default.
3. Recipient sees only information they are permitted to view.
4. Clicking opens the destination entity when permission remains valid.
5. Priority affects presentation ordering, not business correctness.
6. Users may manage preferences for non-critical notifications.
7. Critical financial/verification/security notices should remain mandatory.

---

# Priority Levels

- Critical
- High
- Medium
- Low

---

# Persistence

- Persistent: remains until read/archived/expired
- Transient: may auto-expire quickly
- Mandatory: cannot be fully disabled by preferences

