# Recipient Resolution Rules

1. Role-targeted notifications go to all active users in that business with the role/permission.
2. Assignment-targeted notifications go only to the assigned user (e.g., delivery boy).
3. Creator-targeted notifications always include the initiating user if still active.
4. Removed/suspended users do not receive operational action notifications; owners may receive account notices.
5. Counterparty notifications never include private internal notes.

---

# Preference Rules

| Category | Can Disable |
|---|---|
| Verification / Suspension / Security | No |
| Orders / Deliveries | Rarely (maybe mute low-priority only) |
| Payments / Invoices / Credit Notes | No for core events |
| Marketing/Announcements non-critical | Yes |
| Low stock / Near expiry | Yes with caution defaults on |
| Messages | Mute conversation possible; not system-critical |

---

# Click Behaviour

- If destination entity still visible to recipient → open it.
- If permission lost → show access denied with notification retained.
- If entity deleted/discarded draft → show unavailable message.

